<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernhard II, Duke of Saxe-Meiningen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1800–1882</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernhard II was Duke of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiningen">Meiningen</a> from 1803, under a regency until 1821, to 1866. During his reign the duchy gained additional territory in 1826 and its court culture grew. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a> of 1866 he sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, and after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>'s victory he was forced to abdicate in favour of his son George II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernhard-ii-duke-of-saxe-meiningen.jpg" alt="Bernhard II, Duke of Saxe-Meiningen" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eberhard (photographer) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bernhard_II,_Duke_of_Saxe-Meiningen_Photograph.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
